# Project Overview

- **App:** FinTrack — personal finance + nutrition/macro tracker
- **Stack:** Laravel 12, Inertia.js v2, React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui, PostgreSQL
- **Auth:** Laravel Breeze
- **Testing:** Pest PHP
- **Architecture:** Monolith, SPA-like via Inertia. Two modules: Finance, Nutrition
- **User:** Single user, no multi-tenancy
- **Laravel 12 structure** — no kernel.php

## Directory Conventions

- Pages: `resources/js/Pages/{Module}/`
- Components: `resources/js/Components/{Domain}/{Specific}/`
- Form inputs: `resources/js/Components/Forms/Inputs/{ComponentName}/`
- Hooks: `resources/js/hooks/use{Purpose}.ts`
- Services: `app/Services/{Domain}/` (Finance/, Nutrition/)
- Actions: `app/Actions/`

## Naming Conventions

- Components/classes: PascalCase
- Functions/variables: camelCase
- DB columns/tables: snake_case
- Services: `{Process}Service.php` (e.g., BudgetCalculationService)
- Hooks: `use{Purpose}.ts` (e.g., useJobStatus)
- Types: `interface {Component}Props`
- Event handlers: `handle` prefix (handleClick, handleKeyDown)
- **Always use full descriptive names** — never abbreviations (`$last_name` not `$ln`, `group => group.id` not `g => g.id`)

## Environment

- Windows development — use cmd over PowerShell
- OS-agnostic file path handling in all code
- Security appropriate for personal system — prioritize usability
